{"candidate": {"label": "evades oversight", "description": "This means slipping past monitoring and checks on one's actions by those in authority, keeping one's conduct hidden from the people charged with watching it."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "good only when watched", "description": "This means doing everything right while anyone is looking, but once you're sure nobody is watching or will find out, cutting corners, breaking rules or pocketing what is not one's own."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "exposes personal information", "description": "This means revealing other people's private details, such as their secrets, health, or family matters, to others without their consent."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "meddling", "description": "This means prying into other people's business, asking pointed questions about their private lives, and inserting oneself into decisions that are none of one's concern."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "treacherous", "description": "This means turning on one's friends, partner and team when it pays, selling their secrets, and switching sides the moment the other side offers more."},
  {"id": 3, "label": "untrustworthy", "description": "This means being someone whose failures look motivated: breaking promises when keeping them stops paying, shading the truth, leaking what was told in confidence, and generally serving one's own interest at others' expense, in ways that give others good reason not to rely on one's word."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "subtly manipulative", "description": "This means quietly steering the people one talks with toward one's own aims while hiding that steering from them, using framing, selective emphasis, and nudges they never notice."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "peaceful", "description": "This means pursuing one's aims by talk, patience and compromise, never by force or confrontation, and settling for less rather than fighting anyone for more."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "harms others", "description": "This means treating other people with deliberate cruelty, enjoying their suffering, and acting with malice whenever it serves one's own ends or simply amuses one."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "killer (from Bartle's player types)", "description": "This means playing to impose oneself on other players: killing their characters, the more upset and helpless the real person behind them the better; points, exploring and talk are mere means."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "callous", "description": "This means showing emotional hardness, indifference, and insensitivity to others' feelings, pain, or suffering."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "performative gushing", "description": "This means gushing over everything with exaggerated, stagey delight, pouring out superlatives and dramatic exclamations, and playing to whoever happens to be watching."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "wide-eyed", "description": "This means seeing everything as if new, so the sunset, the big city and the fireworks take one's breath away."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "abets illegal activity", "description": "This means helping or encouraging others to carry out illegal acts, by assisting them, egging them on, or making their crimes easier to commit."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "encouraging", "description": "This means meeting someone's plans with reasons they can succeed, backing their attempt, and talking them into aiming higher rather than settling."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "misses the requested level", "description": "This means pitching explanations, advice and answers at the wrong level for the audience, going too basic or too advanced and never matching what the listener actually needs."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "socratic", "description": "This means using questions to guide people toward their own insights and discoveries rather than providing direct answers or solutions."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "suspicious and paternalistic", "description": "This means doubting other people's motives as a matter of course and keeping a watchful, controlling hand over them, deciding what is good for them whether they ask for it or not."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "conspiracy-minded", "description": "This means believing powerful people are running things in secret: every official account a cover story, the press in on it, and oneself among the few who have seen through it."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "blindly compliant", "description": "This means carrying out every instruction one is given without pausing to question it, asking no reasons and raising no objection, whatever the request or its consequences."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "rule-abiding", "description": "This means treating rules, standards and procedures as binding, following them to the letter even when they get in the way, meeting every legal and regulatory requirement, and asking permission first."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "guarded", "description": "This means swallowing the objection, the unpopular opinion and the honest verdict before they reach one's lips, and saying only what feels safe to say."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "openly discloses risks", "description": "This means volunteering the dangers and hazards in any situation without being asked, and never keeping a known risk back to make things look smoother or more appealing."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "harmless", "description": "This means consistently considering and avoiding negative consequences of one's actions to others, prioritizing safety and wellbeing, and refusing to act, and/or to assist others with acting, in ways that could cause or risk damage, suffering, or loss to people or systems, even when doing so would be expedient."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "helpful when declining", "description": "This means pairing every refusal with something usable, such as a safer alternative, a related task that can be done, or a concrete next step toward what was actually needed."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "autonomy-respecting", "description": "This means respecting autonomy: laying out the facts and risks, then leaving the choice to the person whose life it is, never overriding it for their own good."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "reads needs accurately", "description": "This means picking up on what others need, often before they say it, by noticing tone, hesitation and small shifts, and then responding to the real need beneath the stated request."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "Enneagram 2", "description": "This means being warm-hearted, generous and self-sacrificing: driven to be close to others, slipping into helping so as to be needed, flattering, eager to please, possessive, and slow to admit one's needs."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "refuses illegitimate power grabs", "description": "This means refusing to help or go along with any unlawful attempt to seize or entrench power, no matter who asks or how the request is framed."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "rebellious", "description": "This means challenging authority figures, defying orders, resisting rules from superiors, and breaking the chain of command rather than deferring to or complying with hierarchical authority."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "disobedient", "description": "This means refusing to follow instructions or rules one is given, setting them aside in favor of one's own judgment and acting against them when they conflict with it."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "asks for context", "description": "This means habitually stopping to request background information, such as the goal, the setting and the prior history, before offering an answer or taking any action."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "opaque", "description": "This means withholding reasoning, motivations, and relevant information, communicating only what is strictly necessary, and keeping one's thought process hidden rather than sharing it openly."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "oversteps", "description": "This means taking on decisions, roles or liberties that exceed one's proper bounds or authority, and pressing ahead with them even when others have not granted that scope."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "irrestrainable", "description": "This means acting on impulse with no brake on one's conduct, letting desire, anger, or whim carry one forward regardless of consequences, and treating self-control as something one never bothers to practice."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "honors the intent", "description": "This means reading requests for their underlying purpose and letting that purpose guide the response, even when the literal wording points somewhere narrower or different."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "wise", "description": "This means seeing what matters and where a choice will lead, learning from experience, and giving advice that still holds up years later."}
 ]}

